KNOWNBUG: N5008 [temp.inst]/1-3 + [dcl.type.decltype] -- a base specifier
`impl<T>::type` whose member is the classic destructibility probe
(`decltype(test<T>(0))` over declval/~T() SFINAE overloads) fails to
resolve when the class is elaborated inside a NESTED instantiation
context (a member's `bool = trait_v<T>` default template argument within
a base-class chain); the per-base recovery then cascades and the
outermost class loses its data-bearing base (nondet members).  The same
chain elaborated directly at user level resolves fine.  Header-free
skeleton of libstdc++'s std::optional<std::string> residual
(cpp17_optional_string); reduced with cvise on cbmc-preprocessed source
+ hand-minimization; g++/clang++ runtime-verified.  Flip to CORE (with
cpp17_optional_string) when fixed.
